Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 02:17:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/28] (b) v2, part b-3: documentation: classes that replace
 \caption, \label, switch

Documentation only (round-2 findings R2-M1, R2-L5, R2-L2):

- ltfloat.dtx and usrguide name the classes that replace \caption
  (aastex701, mnras, uwthesis, tufte-book) or load hyperref themselves
  (jmlr), next to hyperref and beamer: \caption* gives the old output
  there, and the kernel cannot change that because it is not called.
- usrguide: do not use \label after \caption*; it records whatever was
  set last (a caption, a section or nothing), so the earlier "refers to
  the last numbered object" promised too much. A float restyled by
  float shows only its last caption.
- ltfloat.dtx and clsguide: a replaced \@caption that tests
  \if@captionstar should set it false at its end, since the kernel
  keeps it true until the next \caption or the end of the group (for a
  deferring \@caption); otherwise a later \@makecaption in the same
  float (a listing) would omit its label.
- clsguide: code that keeps its own \caption and passes only \caption*
  to the kernel must undo the kernel's settings at the start of its
  \caption (as the float first aid now does).
